  "note": "Municipal elections, January 1923. Twenty-six candidates were nominated and four withdrew (Patrick Ferris and Andrew M'Ginn, North Ward; Francis P. Cassidy, South Ward; Arthur Carmichael, West Ward), so there was no contest. The final elected list gives 13 Nationalists and eight Unionists (Belfast News-Letter, 8 January 1923, p. 8; nominations, Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1923, p. 5). Arthur Carmichael (Labour and ex-serviceman) withdrew. Patrick J. M'Laughlin, also nominated for the ward, does not appear in the final elected list, which closes the arithmetic at 13 Nationalists and eight Unionists. Returned unopposed."
